Provider webhooks delivered to the spaces allowed to receive them: one Provider interface in place of per-provider switches, an `event` trigger kind, routing on EDGE, and grants derived from OAuth state. GitHub is the first provider.

This is part 3 of the GitHub sync design (see [plugin-github/spec/SYNC.mdl](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/packages/plugins/plugin-github/spec/SYNC.mdl)). It runs `op:SyncGitHubRepositories`; with events flowing, that operation's poll becomes a slow backstop for missed deliveries. Nothing here is GitHub-specific except `github.ts`.

It spans two repositories: `@dxos/compute` (the trigger kind) and plugin-connector live in `dxos/dxos`; kms-service (which owns the Provider extension point and the webhook ingress) and compute-service (which routes) live in `dxos/edge`.

