## Open questions

Both questions this section held are settled; see D-14.

Efficient polling sync of GitHub repositories and pull requests into ECHO, over one object model.

This is part 1 of a three-part design; each part ships on its own:

| Part | Spec                                              | Needs                          |
|------|---------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| 1    | This document                                     | Nothing                        |
| 2    | [Two-way file sync](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/packages/plugins/plugin-github/spec/FILE-SYNC.mdl)                | Part 1's binding on `Repo`     |
| 3    | [Event dispatch](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/packages/plugins/plugin-connector/spec/EVENTS.mdl) | Part 1's sync operation |

A bound repository is polled every few minutes. A poll that finds nothing costs one conditional request, which GitHub answers `304 Not Modified` without charging the rate limit; a poll that finds changes costs two in the common case (one page of changes, at most 100 pull requests). Once implemented, this document replaces F-4 and F-5 of [PLUGIN.mdl](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/packages/plugins/plugin-github/PLUGIN.mdl).

