## Types

### ECHO schema changes (`@dxos/types`)

`PullRequest` gains five fields and keeps version `0.1.0`. Every new field is optional, so a pull request built from a URL alone (a link preview, an import outside any bound repo) stays valid, and a stored one needs no migration.

```ts
// packages/sdk/types/src/types/PullRequest.ts — fields added by part 1.
export const CheckState = Schema.Literals(['pending', 'success', 'failure', 'neutral']);
export const ReviewDecision = Schema.Literals(['approved', 'changes_requested', 'review_required']);

/** The repository it belongs to; absent on a preview, set by sync and by import. `repo` stays the name string. */
repository: Schema.optional(Ref.Ref(Repo.Repo).annotate({ title: 'Repository' })),
/** Commit at the head branch's tip; the checks below describe this commit. */
headSha: Schema.optional(Schema.String.annotate({ title: 'Head commit' })),
/** Rollup of every check run and status on `headSha`. */
checks: Schema.optional(CheckState.annotate({ title: 'Checks' })),
reviewDecision: Schema.optional(ReviewDecision.annotate({ title: 'Review' })),
/** Issues GitHub will close when it merges (`closingIssuesReferences`). */
closes: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(Ref.Ref(Task.Task)).annotate({ title: 'Closes' })),
```

`TaskSet` gains no field: it stays a use-case agnostic container for `Task`s and milestones. The set that mirrors a repository's issues is found by the foreign key `MaterializeGitHubTarget` already writes to its `Obj.Meta`, which the `Repo` carries too:

```ts
// The issue set for a bound repository: same github.com key as the Repo, no field on TaskSet.
const [issues] = yield* Database.query(Filter.foreignKeys(TaskSet.TaskSet, [{ source: 'github.com', id: repoId }])).run;
```

- **type** `PullRequest` A proposed change to a repository (@dxos/types, 0.1.0).

### Sync state on the binding

The binding is the existing `Cursor` from `@dxos/link`, with `spec.kind: 'external'`. No new ECHO type is needed; this is how part 1 uses its fields.

```ts
// How the GitHub repository binding reads Cursor (packages/core/compute/link/src/Cursor.ts).
type RepoBinding = Cursor.ExternalCursor & {
  /** Epoch milliseconds of the largest `updated_at` the last run saw (`Cursor.formatKey`). */
  max?: string;
  spec: {
    kind: 'external';
    source: Ref.Ref<AccessToken.AccessToken>;
    target: Ref.Ref<Repo.Repo>;
    /** GitHub's numeric repository id, stringified. */
    externalId: string;
    /** ETag of the last `/issues` delta response; sent as `If-None-Match`. */
    token?: string;
    options?: SyncOptions;
    /** Keyed by GitHub numeric id: the last-pulled fields that drive the three-way merge. The repository's
     *  entry also records when the repository and its organization were last read. */
    snapshots?: Record<string, IssueSnapshot | RepoSnapshot>;
  };
};
```

- **type** `SyncOptions` Per-binding options, validated by the connector's optionsSchema.

- **type** `IssueSnapshot` Last-pulled issue fields; unchanged from today's TaskSnapshot.

- **type** `RepoSnapshot` Last-pulled repository fields, and when the repository and its organization were last read.

### GitHub payloads

- **type** `DeltaItem` One item of GET /repos/{o}/{r}/issues?since=…; issues and pull requests share the endpoint.

- **type** `PullRequestDetail` One aliased `pullRequest(number:)` of the batched GraphQL query; everything a PullRequest holds that the delta lacks.

## Services

`GitHubApi` (`src/services/github-api.ts`) gains conditional and batched reads. Existing methods are unchanged.

```ts
// Added to packages/plugins/plugin-github/src/services/github-api.ts.
export type Conditional<A> =
  | { readonly status: 'not-modified' }
  | {
      readonly status: 'ok';
      readonly value: A;
      readonly etag: string | undefined;
      readonly requests: number;
      /** The read stopped at its page cap with pages left. */
      readonly truncated?: boolean;
    };

/**
 * GET /repos/{o}/{r}/issues?state=all&sort=updated&direction=desc&since=…&per_page=100, following `Link`
 * pages. Newest first, so any change reaches page one: If-None-Match goes on that page only, and a 304
 * there means no page changed.
 */
export const listIssuesSince: (
  owner: string,
  repo: string,
  options: { since?: string; etag?: string; direction?: 'asc' | 'desc'; maxPages?: number },
) => GitHubEffect<Conditional<readonly DeltaItem[]>>;

/** One GraphQL query of one repository, one aliased `pullRequest(number:)` per number; at most 100 per call. */
export const fetchPullRequestDetails: (
  owner: string,
  repo: string,
  numbers: readonly number[],
) => GitHubEffect<readonly PullRequestDetail[]>;

/** GET /repos/{o}/{r} with If-None-Match. */
export const fetchRepoConditional: (
  owner: string,
  repo: string,
  etag?: string,
) => GitHubEffect<Conditional<GitHubRepo>>;
```

- **service** `GitHubApi` Typed GitHub REST and GraphQL client bound to one access token.

## Operations

- **op** `MaterializeGitHubTarget` Find or create the Repo for a selected repository, keyed by its GitHub id, and the TaskSet that mirrors its issues.

- **op** `SyncGitHubRepositories` Run one poll for every binding of the connection: the delta, the pull-request batch, the three-way merge and push for issues, and the cursor advance.

- **type** `SyncResult`

## Features

- **feat** `F-1` One object per GitHub item
  - `F-1.1` A binding's Cursor targets a Repo, found or created by its github.com foreign key.
  - `F-1.2` A pull request is one PullRequest object with `repository` set, whether it arrived by sync, by import or from a link opened in the space.
  - `F-1.3` An issue is a Task in the TaskSet that carries the bound Repo's github.com foreign key; TaskSet itself has no repository field.
  - `F-1.4` ImportPullRequest names a pull request in a bound repository → it returns the synced PullRequest, without a request to GitHub
  - `F-1.5` a space holds a Task mirrored from a pull request by the earlier sync → the first sync that reads the pull request replaces it with a PullRequest carrying the same foreign key, and drops it from every TaskSet and parent…

- **feat** `F-2` Delta polling
  - `F-2.1` a binding is polled → the first request is listIssuesSince with since = Cursor.max and etag = Cursor.spec.token
  - `F-2.2` the delta answers 304, no open PullRequest of the binding has `checks` = pending, and the Repo description has no local edit → the run ends for that binding after one request, and Cursor.lastTick advances
  - `F-2.3` the delta returns items → every item with `pull_request` is fetched in fetchPullRequestDetails batches of at most 100
  - `F-2.4` An open pull request whose `checks` is `pending` joins the batch on every poll, a poll whose delta answers 304 included, until it settles, because check results do not change `updated_at`.
  - `F-2.5` Cursor.max advances once every page of the delta is applied, so an interrupted run re-reads from the last complete watermark.
  - `F-2.6` The repository itself is read with fetchRepoConditional, and its milestones with it whether or not the repository answers 304, at most once an hour per binding, so neither is part of the one-request quiet poll; the repo…
  - `F-2.8` a binding has no stored ETag yet (its first sync, or a backfill still in progress) → the delta is read oldest first, at most 10 pages a run; a run that stops at the cap advances Cursor.max, stores no ETag and asks to ru…
  - `F-2.7` Issues keep today's three-way merge and push of title, description and status; pull requests are pull-only.

- **feat** `F-3` Scheduling
  - `F-3.1` The GitHub connector entry sets `trigger` to a timer with a default schedule of every 3 minutes and `remote: true`, so polls run on EDGE with no client open.
  - `F-3.2` RefreshPullRequests and its hourly trigger skip every pull request in a bound repository, which its binding's poll covers; they remain only for pull requests imported from repositories no binding targets.
  - `F-3.3` useSyncPullRequest stays as a refresh-on-open for pull requests in spaces with no binding.

